#N canvas 20 20 1500 1150 12;
#X text 20 20 e_gigaverb -- the reverb's gigaverb \, one of e_verb's three engines (Brendan \, 2026-11-05): ELSE's giga.rev~ \, Juhana Sadeharju's Gigaverb: early reflections \, diffusers and a four-line feedback delay network \, in a room of 25 square meters. Its two sides are summed: mono. ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: c_kit's \$0 \, for the throw. arg 2: e_verb's \$0 \, for its input. In: the sends \, on e_verb's \$2-in. inlet: want <1 or 0> \, size <0-100> and damping <0-100> \, from e_verb. Out: the reverb alone \, thrown to c_kit's \$1-out. outlet: 1 or 0 as its switch~ turns., f 70;
#X obj 700 300 inlet;
#X obj 700 340 route want size damping;
#X obj 700 380 t f f;
#X obj 840 460 * 0.21694;
#X obj 20 300 r~ \$2-in;
#X obj 20 340 *~ 0;
#X obj 700 460 e_tail;
#X obj 700 500 t f f;
#X obj 700 560 switch~;
#X obj 840 560 outlet;
#X obj 840 420 f;
#X obj 1000 380 t b f f;
#X obj 1000 420 expr 0.3436 * pow(20\, -0.307 * \$f1 / 100);
#X obj 20 460 else/giga.rev~ -size 25 -decay 2.578 -damp 0.3 -bw 0.7 -dry 0 -early 0.25 -late 1 -spread 0.5;
#X obj 20 560 throw~ \$1-out;
#X obj 300 560 env~ 4096 2048;
#X obj 700 640 expr 0.5765 * pow(20\, \$f1 / 100);
#X msg 700 680 decay \$1;
#X obj 900 640 * 0.006;
#X msg 900 680 damp \$1;
#X msg 1000 300 clear;
#X text 700 760 size is Gigaverb's decay \, in seconds: 1.153 times the time e_verb's size reads \, so that the tail measures it \, 0.5 s at 0 to 10 s at 100 \, even in ratio. Its room stays 25: changing it moves every delay. damping is its own \, 0 to 0.6 \, so the tail darkens as freeverb's does at the same damping: at 1 it has none. Each starts at 50 in its boxes: c_steps tells c_kit every value at load. ELSE's objects go by folder \, else/giga.rev~ \, and this one creates silently under -nogui. Its dry sound is off \, its early reflections a quarter of its tail \, as the research heard it. The gain matches its level to the plate's \, falling as size grows \, since a longer tail makes gigaverb louder than it makes the plate., f 50;
#X text 20 640 The engine's own: the input at its gain while it is wanted and 0 once it is not \, so a type changed away from rings out on what it already holds \; e_tail turns its switch~ on while it is wanted and off once its tail has died \, clearing its delay lines \, and the outlet tells e_verb \, whose own switch~ is on while any engine is., f 50;
